# THE AL FREE FUNCTIONS THAT ARE WRITTEN RATHER THAN GENERATED, and nothing else, live here.
#
# `bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters` is ON everywhere in this tree and stays on -- `TableId`,
# `FieldNo` and `EntryNo` are all int32 and AL swaps them silently, which is what the strong types
# are for. It is switched off in this ONE directory because the finding here is not a defect: the
# signatures are AL's own. `ConvertStr(String: Text, FromCharacters: Text, ToCharacters: Text)` is
# `methods-auto/text/text-convertstr-text-text-method.md`, and a type invented to tell the second
# from the third would break the name equality the documentation check hangs on -- CLAUDE.md's
# first architectural invariant. `Field.Get(TableNo, No)` is the same case: both are declared
# `Integer` in `devenv-field-virtual-table.md`. `TableId` and `FieldNo` exist and are the right
# types EVERYWHERE ELSE; at this boundary the signature is AL's.
#
# It is a directory rather than a NOLINT because a NOLINT costs a number in `test/todo-baseline`,
# and that number may only fall. It is narrowed to a directory rather than to `src/rt` because a
# directory whose whole contents are AL signatures is the narrowest point available -- the same
# move as `misc-include-cleaner.IgnoreHeaders` in the root config, at the same scale.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters
